      "description": "Traditional ballet costumes, such as leotards and tutus, are designed to emphasize grace and movement. The use of a ballet costume on a man who does not conform to the physical norms of ballet creates a humorous juxtaposition, relying on the viewer's understanding of ballet aesthetics and norms.",
